=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play updates/by-hardn-debian ---------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: updates/by-hardn-debian$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. debian-installer after$
# hardn's Enable: the package, hardn's file and the record.$
# Disable deletes the file, then purges the package.$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured unattended-upgrades$
$
  Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  unattended-upgrades  Installed$
   -  Upgrades             Daily by 52hardn-auto-upgrades$
   -  Package Lists        Daily by 52hardn-auto-upgrades$
   -  Upgrade Timer        On apt-daily-upgrade.timer$
   -  Lists Timer          On apt-daily.timer$
   -  Turned on by         hardn record of 2026-10-20$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable automatic updates$
      Undo hardn's changes$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
  Checking the host...$
$
# Disable automatic updates ####################################$
$
  Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  Auto Updates         Off$
   -  python3-dbus         Kept apt autoremove removes it$
   -  python3-distro-info  Kept apt autoremove removes it$
   -  Rollback             Reinstalls from the repositories$
  [ ] Rollback             Turns updates on by 20auto-upgrades$
$
   -  Turn off daily upgrades$
      /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52hardn-auto-upgrades$
      @@ -1,3 +0,0 @@$
      -// Written by hardn (Auto Updates).$
      -APT::Periodic::Update-Package-Lists "1";$
      -APT::Periodic::Unattended-Upgrade "1";$
$
   -  Remove unattended-upgrades$
      unattended-upgrades$
      -installed$
      +purged, with 20auto-upgrades$
      $ apt-get purge -y unattended-upgrades$
$
   -  Delete hardn's record$
      /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json$
$
  Turn automatic updates off? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Turn off daily upgrades     Done$
  [+] Remove unattended-upgrades  Done$
  [+] Delete hardn's record       Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52hardn-auto-upgrades,$
  /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/20auto-upgrades,$
  /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50unattended-upgrades,$
  /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured no unattended-upgrades$
$
  Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] unattended-upgrades  Not installed$
  [ ] Upgrades             Off unset$
  [ ] Package Lists        Off unset$
   -  Upgrade Timer        On apt-daily-upgrade.timer$
   -  Lists Timer          On apt-daily.timer$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Install unattended-upgrades$
$
